From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:41:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/isa/lpc_ich9: add an x-device-id property

Proprietary Intel GOP drivers, run from an option ROM for a passed-through
iGPU, read the device ID of the LPC bridge at 00:1f.0 and refuse to start
unless it belongs to a PCH they know. q35's ICH9 reports 0x2918, which none
of them accept, so the display stays dark through the UEFI phase.

x-device-id sets the device ID that ICH9-LPC reports:

    -global ICH9-LPC.x-device-id=0xa082

The default, 0, keeps 0x2918. The ID is applied at realize, before anything
reads it.

A real PCH ID does not match q35's ACPI tables and power management, and
some guest graphics drivers choose their quirks by PCH, so set it only for
firmware that needs it. vfio's x-igd-lpc cannot help on q35: it creates its
own LPC bridge at 00:1f.0, which ICH9 already occupies.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [upstream leaves the IDs of q35's ICH9 alone, see docs/igd-assign.txt]
Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
---
 hw/isa/lpc_ich9.c             |  6 ++++++
 include/hw/southbridge/ich9.h | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/isa/lpc_ich9.c b/hw/isa/lpc_ich9.c
index edf9783..c946218 100644
--- a/hw/isa/lpc_ich9.c
+++ b/hw/isa/lpc_ich9.c
@@ -712,6 +712,11 @@ static void ich9_lpc_realize(PCIDevice *d, Error **errp)
     ISABus *isa_bus;
     uint32_t irq;
 
+    /* Before anything reads the device ID; see device_id_override. */
+    if (lpc->device_id_override != 0) {
+        pci_config_set_device_id(d->config, lpc->device_id_override);
+    }
+
     if ((lpc->smi_host_features & BIT_ULL(ICH9_LPC_SMI_F_CPU_HOT_UNPLUG_BIT)) &&
         !(lpc->smi_host_features & BIT_ULL(ICH9_LPC_SMI_F_CPU_HOTPLUG_BIT))) {
         /*
@@ -845,6 +850,7 @@ static const Property ich9_lpc_properties[] = {
                      pm.swsmi_timer_enabled, true),
     DEFINE_PROP_BOOL("x-smi-periodic-timer", ICH9LPCState,
                      pm.periodic_timer_enabled, true),
+    DEFINE_PROP_UINT16("x-device-id", ICH9LPCState, device_id_override, 0),
 };
 
 static void ich9_send_gpe(AcpiDeviceIf *adev, AcpiEventStatusBits ev)
diff --git a/include/hw/southbridge/ich9.h b/include/hw/southbridge/ich9.h
index 2c35dd0..9b299cf 100644
--- a/include/hw/southbridge/ich9.h
+++ b/include/hw/southbridge/ich9.h
@@ -54,6 +54,16 @@ struct ICH9LPCState {
     uint8_t rst_cnt;
     MemoryRegion rst_cnt_mem;
 
+    /*
+     * PCI device ID to report instead of the class default (0x2918), set
+     * with the x-device-id property; 0 keeps the default. Proprietary Intel
+     * GOP drivers refuse to start unless the LPC bridge is a PCH they know.
+     * A real PCH ID does not match the q35 ACPI tables and power management,
+     * and it changes which quirks some guest graphics drivers apply, so set
+     * it only for firmware that needs it.
+     */
+    uint16_t device_id_override;
+
     /* SMI feature negotiation via fw_cfg */
     uint64_t smi_host_features;       /* guest-invisible, host endian */
     uint8_t smi_host_features_le[8];  /* guest-visible, read-only, little
